  "currentRoundInspection": {
    "inspectedOn": "2026-10-15",
    "scope": "Two actually inspected2009 whole oblique/elevated exterior photographs,plus standard viewer PMTiles/DEM only.No bespoke plans/surveys.Reference photos viewed only,not redistributed;fine sculpture/tracery approximated geometrically.",
    "pictures": [
      {
        "page": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Neuer_Dom_Linz.jpg",
        "author": "H. Raab (Vesta)",
        "date": "2009-05-18",
        "license": "CC-BY-SA-3.0",
        "observed": "Actually inspected whole eastern oblique including lower facade. Warm light-stone Gothic body,polygonal chapel/choir envelope,large projecting transept with pointed rose/tracery window,row of lower lights,deep pointed timber portal and ornamental gable. Gray-green standing-seam copper nave/transept roofs have small dormer rhythms. Stepped buttresses/flying arches and pinnacles carry the silhouette. Tall single northern stone tower has tapering octagonal belfry,open Gothic crown and ribbed stone spire/finial. Fine sculpture/rose lobes/inscriptions simplified."
      },
      {
        "page": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Neuer_Dom_Linz_(DFdB).JPG",
        "author": "Dein Freund der Baum",
        "date": "2009-06-15",
        "license": "CC-BY-SA-3.0",
        "observed": "Actually inspected elevated whole cathedral from a city rooftop. Single very tall stone north tower dominates long steep gray-green nave roof;lower tower has staged buttresses and large pointed belfry openings. Open/cusped crown precedes the long narrow ribbed stone spire. Much smaller dark open metal fleche rises at crossing. Narrow clerestory bays and low side-aisle windows/buttresses repeat along the long body. Exact small roof/crocket rhythm and hidden western entry canopy remain approximate. Photograph finish/date retained;current finish not independently surveyed."
      }
    ]
  }
